  "body": "Held for over 35 years, 258 Okura River Road comes to market, offering two retreat-like homes hidden on an all-encompassing two-acre lifestyle block within reach of the city, coast and local conveniences.\r\n\r\nMulti-generational families gain a rare advantage here: a place to disappear from the world yet stay well connected. House loved ones, host guests in privacy, explore an income, or simply keep it all to yourself.\r\n\r\nBehind automatic gates, the three-level main residence gently reveals itself, offering understated luxury, comfort and peace, framed by tranquil grounds and a sea glimpse between the palms.\r\n\r\nAt its heart, the sitting area, generous kitchen, dining and living zones flow together. Take in the landscape from the elevated deck, or retreat to the gas fire beneath the grapevines. This level also holds a guest powder room, laundry and the primary suite, with its office, lavish ensuite and walk-in wardrobe. Upstairs, a second master suite and balcony claim the top floor.\r\n\r\nDownstairs, a games room with a kitchen, a bedroom and a bathroom nearing completion give guests or teenagers privacy. Smart lighting extends to the tennis court floodlights, and a double garage with internal access completes the picture.\r\n\r\nThe second home pairs cottage charm with genuine scale: two bedrooms, open-plan living that flows outdoors, and a third living space beneath a sloping ceiling. A six-car garage with a workshop will delight collectors, and a studio suits a gym or golf simulator.\r\n\r\nNatives, exotic palms, rolling lawns, a pond and fruit trees create a quiet refuge, complete with a pool, tennis court and putting green of your own.\r\n\r\nAlbany is close by, Long Bay Regional Park makes an easy beach outing, and the Oteha Valley on-ramp links you to the city. Zoned for Long Bay School, Northcross Intermediate and Long Bay College.\r\n\r\nThis one-of-a-kind address is ready for its next chapter. Call us to register your interest.",
